SECTION D.  THE GENERALISATION -- a holonomic auxiliary attaches TWO ways, and they are opposite
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [PASS] D1  PARALLEL Schur (L44's arrangement): eliminating an auxiliary that mixes with the dangerous variable ADDS  A^2/D  to its coefficient -- STIFFNESSES ADD, so it RAISES A FLOOR   (h_qq -> h_qq + A^2/D; with h_qq = 0 (marginal) this is exactly L44's a_UV = A^2/(4D + 24E4 z^2))
  [PASS] D2  SERIES Schur: putting the dangerous function on the AUXILIARY and tying it back with a quadratic spring gives the HARMONIC combination -- COMPLIANCES ADD, so it LOWERS A CEILING   (1/Sigma_eff = 1/Sigma + 1/lambda, with f'' = 2 Sigma.  Also a Schur complement of an ALGEBRAIC auxiliary -- the same technique, attached the other way round.)
  [PASS] D2b and the series form is EXACTLY the harmonic rule 1/Sigma_eff = 1/Sigma + 1/lambda
  [PASS] D3  THEOREM (the reason the technique has not applied a second time): a PARALLEL Schur shift is a FINITE rank-one addition A^2/D, so it CANNOT render a DIVERGENT coefficient finite; making the shift itself divergent requires D -> 0, at which point the auxiliary's own Hessian entry vanishes, its equation becomes the CONSTRAINT A v = 0, and it DELETES the mode instead of repairing it   (so: PARALLEL repairs a ZERO (L44's case), SERIES repairs an INFINITY (C-L1's case).  The programme's outstanding sore point needs the arrangement nobody has tried.)
  [PASS] D3b and the two arrangements are NOT interchangeable, computed: at Sigma = 1e16 the PARALLEL shift leaves 1e16 + A^2/D (no repair) while the SERIES shift returns lambda Sigma/(Sigma+lambda) < lambda (repaired)   (parallel: 1e16 -> 1.0000000000000001e16 with A^2/D = 100.  series: 1e16 -> 9999.99999999999 with lambda = 1e4.)
  [PASS] D4  MODE COUNT: an auxiliary with NO derivatives on it adds ZERO propagating modes -- its own equation is algebraic -- PROVIDED its Hessian is invertible; if the Hessian degenerates the auxiliary becomes a multiplier and the count CHANGES   (the invertibility condition and the definite-sign condition are the SAME condition.  Any auxiliary given a kinetic term instead adds +1 (scalar) or +3 (vector) modes, taking the deposited theory from 4 to 5 or 7 against a stated requirement of 2.)

